		{"id":"0b1c2802ec6b9646","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/Part_04/2.08-Transformation.md","x":3840,"y":-165,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"d19621b68400a31d","type":"text","text":"\"I've heard vampire pregnancies take longer.\" Lilith said.\n\n\"You aren't sure?\"\n\n\"Well I've never been pregnant myself. So no.\"\n\n\"Don't want kids?\" Sara asked.\n\n\"I do, it's just... not been the right time yet.\"\n\nSara rubbed her belly and nodded, \"Timing is everything, that's for sure.\" ","x":1280,"y":280,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"aed17f8553169183","type":"text","text":"\"You could move to Forgotten Hollow, if you want to. It would certainly make things easier for you and the new little one.\" Lilith pointed out.\n\n\"It might make things easier for me,\" Sarah shifted in her seat, \"But my two older daughters are human. I'm not sure If they would be happy there.\" \n\nI guess basically like setting this up as a scene that shows how like Sara was aware that they didn't have to stay in a human dominated area and pretend to be normal when they weren't, but like she actively chose to stay in a human area for her daughters mainly. Like, later on, Savanna has this thing of like, we pretended to be normal when we weren't. Yeah, and the alternative was acknowledging that we weren't normal, moving to somewhere where people aren't normal, and making you deal with living around even more occult creatures. Like, no one's gonna say that to Savanna, but that's basically gonna be the reality of the situation. Sara's choices were pretend to be kinda human and try to blend in even though she's a vampire, or move to somewhere like Forgotten Hollow and embrace being a vampire and make her two human daughters just deal with the fact that they're surrounded by supernatural creatures all the time. And Sara doesn't see it as pretending anyway. But whatever. I don't know how to phrase it. Sara chose living among humans and blending in with humans for herself over trying to make her two human daughters blend in with vampires.\n\nI don't know if it would be Lilith to point this out or someone else or something like that. I don't know. But still, I would like it to come up at some point that like, yeah, it would be easier for Sara if she moved, but it's easier for her daughters if she doesn't, so she doesn't. ","x":2120,"y":560,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"b75ea10407f3b748","type":"text","text":"Sara could hardly believe it, she was pregnant by Jane a **second** time. Sara kissed her wife again. They were going to have another child. \n\nSure, that odd rejecting sensation was probably going to return, along with all the stretching and pain. But it would all be worth dealing with that. Besides, this time, Jane already knew about it. And even when she hadn't, Jane had still help Sara cope with it. Between her excitement and touch, they would get through it together. ","x":640,"y":280,"width":400,"height":400}
	],
	"edges":[]
}